---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Banner from '../components/Banner.astro';
import bannerToby from '../assets/photos/general/toby-stepping-stones.jpg';
import VideoEmbed from '../components/VideoEmbed.astro';
import { FILMS, CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../site';

/**
 * Placeholder structure — Toby's copy to come (brief, "Site structure").
 * Everything inside .placeholder is scaffolding text to be replaced; the
 * headings and the video slot are the structure worth keeping.
 */
---

<Base
  title="Background"
  description="Toby Wise — a career in banking and consulting, then back to the hills. Why Second Summit exists."
>
  <Banner
    image={bannerToby}
    alt="Toby crossing a river on stepping stones, pack on, poles out"
    focal="center 30%"
    desktopAspect="16 / 9"
    priority
  />

  <section style="padding-bottom:16px">
    <div class="eyebrow">The background</div>
    <h1 class="sub">Toby Wise, FRGS</h1>
  </section>

  <section>
    <VideoEmbed
      id={FILMS.background.id}
      kicker={FILMS.background.kicker}
      title={FILMS.background.title}
      wide
    />
    <p class="small" style="padding-top:8px">
      Piece-to-camera film sits here, with the written version beneath it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="placeholder">
      <p>
        I spent my career in banking and consulting. A couple of years ago I started walking
        seriously again, and found I didn't want to stop. Second Summit is the result: long routes,
        walked self-supported, planned carefully and filmed as I go.
      </p>
      <p>
        In March I walked the Coast to Coast — 174 miles from the Irish Sea to the North Sea, camping
        high and sleeping in old pubs. This October it's the northern half of the Snowdonia Way. What
        comes after that, I'll decide when I'm back.
      </p>
    </div>

    <blockquote>The first summit was work. This is the second.</blockquote>

    <div class="placeholder">
      <p>
        If you're at a similar stage — the career largely done, wondering what fills the space — this
        site is partly for you. The routes, the kit that worked and didn't, the honest account of
        what a 54-year-old body can be trained to do. In time I'd like to tell other people's
        second-summit stories here too, not just mine.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p style="margin-top:12px">
      Fellow of the Royal Geographical Society. Trustee of the Gwennili Sailing Trust, which takes
      veterans offshore under sail.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="eyebrow">The walks</div>
    <p>
      <a href="/coast-to-coast/">Coast to Coast</a> — 174 miles, March 2026, walked self-supported.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/snowdonia-way/">Snowdonia Way</a> — 44 miles, October 2026, tracked live.
    </p>
    <p class="small" style="padding-top:8px">
      Ben walked the final days of the Coast to Coast: <a href="/wise-brothers/">the Wise Brothers</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="eyebrow">Partners</div>
    <p class="small">
      If your brand fits this world and you'd like to talk,{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>get in touch →</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
